1
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:06,300
I carry high my craven flag,

2
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:11,277
my ally I'm gonna fly and let my
struggles shoot me through the sky!

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:14,997
It'd be a pity if we
lingered here and let our

4
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:18,057
pretty sparks of life
blend aloud and disappear?

5
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:24,457
There may be fog that even you can't
navigate If someone strong like you is lost,

6
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:25,837
then who will set me straight?

7
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,837
Cause when the waves cast my heart adrift.

8
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,737
It's been your kindness and your strength.

9
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:33,017
That would free me from the mist.

10
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,840
And just like that.

11
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,800
We move on.

12
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:40,457
Sail to a new dawn.

13
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:43,297
Weigh anchor right as high as you can.

14
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:45,437
I assure I don't need anger.

15
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,577
I go fast as I am, yeah.

16
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:50,657
I hear you laughing like
you're numb to it all.

17
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:52,617
While we're dashing together.

18
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,097
No, we're never gonna fall, you know.

19
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,657
The whole world may now be my enemy.

20
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:00,197
Water's slow, but I ain't backing down.

21
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,157
So long as I'm free, yeah.

22
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,137
Thought I'd give it, come
round the current with me.

23
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:07,697
All in, wake up bright and early.

24
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:09,800
Making for the peak we go.

25
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:22,197
All in, wake up bright and early.

26
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:24,340
Making for the peak we go.

27
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:41,440
Having fun?

28
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:45,680
Yeah, this is the best
day ever! Hey, you guys!

29
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:47,617
I found some shaved ice right over there!

30
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:48,530
Let's go!

31
00:01:48,613 --> 00:01:49,620
Papaya, fly!

32
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:53,057
I've never had shaved ice
before, that sounds so neat!

33
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:56,120
We gotta go, Nami! Come on!

34
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,960
Hurry, hurry!

35
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,580
What if it melts?

36
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,300
They've got a ton of flavors!

37
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,320
Oh, how do I pick?

38
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,060
Wait, I know!

39
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,120
I want red bean soup flavor!

40
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,200
How fast things!

41
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,920
There's no end to this.

42
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:34,780
I know you told me to go,
but I can't leave you.

43
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:38,460
You must!

44
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:41,457
Momonosuke, I don't understand.

45
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:43,658
Why won't you let me help you fight?

46
00:02:43,780 --> 00:02:46,120
This matter is ours to settle, Yamato.

47
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,520
Step back!

48
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:02,000
Stop wasting my time!

49
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:04,740
Just bring me Straw Hat, little baby!

50
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:06,690
Uh-huh!

51
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:08,700
Curts of a ring!

52
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:14,440
I'll end this! Sneak pole!

53
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:15,836
Scrolling Chouchou!

54
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:23,970
FIRE!

55
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:25,200
EXCEPT!

56
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,020
Burn to ashes!

57
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:36,640
You baby scum!

58
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:43,780
Just kidding.

59
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:52,120
FIRE BREAK FORWARD!

60
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:57,140
I'm an Admiral of the Navy,
you arrogant little dope!

61
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:02,200
You think I could rise to that position
with such an obvious weakness?!

62
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:14,180
Water gives life to humans and the
rest of the natural world as well.

63
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,820
I'll show you.

64
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:18,480
What are you doing?!

65
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,070
Rhyzo!

66
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:31,940
We need a new plan!

67
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,637
His branches keep growing back!

68
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,940
Hold on, I'm coming!

69
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:43,740
Think, Cat, he must have some weakness!

70
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:47,099
Maybe if we cut all of his
branches at once somehow!

71
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,330
Rwahahahaha!

72
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:00,790
Wominosuke...

73
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:01,990
Why?

74
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:05,290
Rwahahahaha!

75
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:10,970
Hidden stairs?

76
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,590
Oh!

77
00:05:17,673 --> 00:05:18,666
Seems we've been sniffed out.

78
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,597
You were with the rest of the crew,
so naturally I got suspicious.

79
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,915
Don't act like I'm some kind of hyena.

80
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:27,280
Do watch your step.

81
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,240
It's a bit moldy down here.

82
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:35,380
I tried to hide this route from
Orochi and Kaido, to no avail.

83
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:38,996
As you know, their lead
performer, Jack, is a fishman.

84
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:43,060
So despite my best efforts, they
found the polyglyph in no time.

85
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:46,227
What does being a fishman
have to do with it?

86
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,760
You'll see soon enough.

87
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,920
This is a lot of stares.

88
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,917
How far down are you going to take us?

89
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:55,700
How far a few hundred
years or so I suppose.

90
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:03,520
Mr Tang where was that light coming from?

91
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,577
There's a glass window that lets you look

92
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:12,400
outside you can take a
quick peek if you like.

93
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:16,994
We're already at the bottom of the sea.

94
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,480
That's cheating.

95
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:29,340
Can you see out there?

96
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:41,080
A whole city underwater?

97
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:48,960
That's the land of Wano from
about 800 years in the past.

98
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:51,140
The original, you might say.

99
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,300
Eight hundred years ago.

100
00:06:58,620 --> 00:07:00,032
What happened back then?

101
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,861
A fine question.

102
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:06,520
I understand the how and the
when, but the why is lost to time.

103
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:13,833
The reason it's so well preserved is
because that's not actually seawater.

104
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:16,420
This is what I do know.

105
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:21,487
The land of Wano was once located at a
base of a huge mountain called Fujiyama.

106
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,941
At one point, walls were created,

107
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:27,198
enclosing the island, causing
rainfall to accumulate.

108
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:28,560
As time passed,

109
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:30,077
the town became Unbelievable,

110
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:33,517
so the people moved up the
mountain and built a new country,

111
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,541
far above what you're seeing now.

112
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,313
And that's the modern-day land of Juana?

113
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:41,690
Exactly.

114
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:49,373
Here's our destination.

115
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,400
A road poneglyph.

116
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:11,417
This is the third one that
we've found on our journey.

117
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,700
Just one more.

118
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:15,475
And we can make our way to Laugh Tale.

119
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:21,369
We're in a small cave at the foot of
Fujiyama, where the water doesn't reach.

120
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,897
This isn't the only
thing buried down here.

121
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:30,617
It is said the ancient weapon
Pluton lies further beneath us.

122
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:36,937
I've never seen the weapon myself and
I'm afraid I can't show it to you now.

123
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:40,697
In order to retrieve
it the giant walls must

124
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:43,657
first be removed opening
the borders of Wano.

125
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:46,497
Not only lowers our defenses but unleashes

126
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:49,168
the power of an ancient
weapon on the world.

127
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:59,637
How frightful that is
quite the risk but that was

128
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:02,277
Odin's wish why would he
want that for this country.

129
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:07,677
Well I've told you everything that was

130
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:10,757
passed down to me I haven't a clue what.

131
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:14,722
Odin learned to cross the sea, so
his intentions remain a mystery.

132
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:22,950
Strupee!

133
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,100
Hey, Beppo!

134
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:34,580
The shaved ice here is great!
What? Where? I need it!

135
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:35,580
I need it now!

136
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:51,020
Leave our country alone!

137
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:52,940
Lord Babonosuke!

138
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,340
You're only human.

139
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:58,780
You're no match for Mother Nature.

140
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,100
By the way,

141
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:05,026
in case you haven't caught on yet, the
reason I'm here is because Kaido is gone.

142
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:07,160
He was a deterrent.

143
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:12,380
Even if he ran this country into the
ground, But he kept your enemies at bay.

144
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:17,700
But lucky for you, we're not
planning to invade right now.

145
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:22,500
So if you want me to go away,
then bring me Straw Hat Luffy!

146
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,430
Momonosuke!

147
00:10:25,513 --> 00:10:27,080
Call the Straw Hats now!

148
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:29,475
It'll be fine, they won't lose to him!

149
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:35,500
I cannot do that!

150
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,030
Huh?

151
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:40,341
It's the same reason why
I cannot ask you for aid.

152
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:44,335
You've spent your entire life
imprisoned on Onigashima.

153
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:47,000
But now, you can finally be free.

154
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:49,422
So I will send you off properly.

155
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:54,417
I've been depending on Luffy and his
friends to see me through these trials.

156
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:58,441
But we who remain in this country
must be able to stand on our own.

157
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:03,060
We cannot rely on those who are departing.

158
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,557
This is our country to protect.

159
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:08,920
We must drive out its
enemies with our own power!

160
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,110
Momonosuke.

161
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:14,800
Get out of here, you monster!

162
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,030
Why?

163
00:11:22,113 --> 00:11:23,680
Why must you fail me now?

164
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:28,860
Gotta say, you're a pretty
pathetic excuse for a dragon.

165
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:32,000
I've had just about enough
of your stupid games.

166
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:41,960
Leave this country!

167
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,680
It finally worked!

168
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,540
That's the power of our lord!

169
00:11:57,780 --> 00:12:00,662
He already wields that
attack like Kaido himself!

170
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,080
I said go!

171
00:12:02,660 --> 00:12:03,490
No!

172
00:12:03,573 --> 00:12:05,380
The water will never come back!

173
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:07,890
Dammit!

174
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,280
You little brats!

175
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,720
Drop them out!

176
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,280
He's doing it!

177
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:16,900
He has the full power of a dragon now!

178
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:20,680
Perhaps, but his aim still
leaves much to be desired.

179
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:50,680
Damn, kid.

180
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:52,460
What the hell?

181
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:55,520
You trying to burn down the whole city?

182
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:56,960
You want to fight?

183
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,220
Fine by me.

184
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:01,659
You really think I'm scared
of some kind of wannabe?

185
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:05,640
Try that again and I'll
skewer you from head to tail!

186
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,600
Why can't I move?

187
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:24,540
Conqueror's Haki...

188
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,374
Who the hell is there?

189
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:36,840
No it can't be the red hair
pirates why are they here

190
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:42,957
Come on boss you can't just
bust your Haki out without

191
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:47,457
warning the new recruits can't
handle it Yet I'm not saying

192
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:52,097
you have to be nice mr marine
but these pirates fought hard

193
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:55,377
to change history Don't you
think you'd be in a poor sport,

194
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:58,931
stomping out flowers before
you know what color they bloom?

195
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:02,160
Does this new era frighten you so much?

196
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,820
Is that why?

197
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:09,480
Listen, I'm not trying to fight you guys.

198
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:10,740
At least not yet.

199
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,740
Yeah, all right, I get it.

200
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:16,940
It worked!

201
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:19,237
You did it, Momonosuke!

202
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,197
I think he's leaving!

203
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:23,398
You've defended the land of
Wano, just like you said!

204
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:26,120
I can protect this country.

205
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,220
I can protect my home.

206
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:39,980
Of course!

207
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,339
You're incredible!

208
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,620
He ran away.

209
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,880
You did pretty good, Momo.

210
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:48,400
Look at that.

211
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:49,658
They don't need us.

212
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:56,377
I assume the rest of you felt
that overwhelming Haki here.

213
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:59,020
Yeah, that sure was crazy, wasn't it?

214
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:07,720
Made me think of an old friend for a sec

215
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:16,900
Are you all right?

216
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:19,260
Shinobu Raizo

217
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:26,099
They just need fluids and some rest
they'll be better soon I promise.

218
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:31,397
That is a relief he was
right I hate to agree

219
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,357
with him but the whole world feared Kaido.

220
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:38,420
As long as he held Wano in his iron grip
no one would dare set foot on his shores.

221
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:42,337
Forgive me to my great
shame I was in cutie at

222
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:45,180
the time and wholly
ignorant of your struggle.

223
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:49,677
It all worked out fine
nobody blames you Karoo.

224
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:52,597
Lord Momonosuke really put in the work.

225
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,560
He saved us all.

226
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:58,760
By the way, how is Otsuru?

227
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:00,137
It's been quite a while.

228
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:02,757
She's hurt, but she will live.

229
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:05,557
She was burned when Okobore Town set fire.

230
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:07,287
I failed to protect her too.

231
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:10,557
There you are, Otsuru.

232
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:14,577
I heard King came back to see you. He did.

233
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:17,517
He had to hurry back to
the Flower Capital though.

234
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,020
You're from the capital, too, dear.

235
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,260
Go be with your love. I will.

236
00:16:22,700 --> 00:16:23,620
And soon.

237
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:25,742
I've waited long enough already.

238
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:34,086
You know, even after 20 years, she's as
beautiful as she was on our wedding day.

239
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:35,090
All right.

240
00:16:35,173 --> 00:16:36,200
Enough mushy stuff.

241
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,829
You're becoming even
more of a dog than me.

242
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:42,842
It's all right.

243
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,180
I think it's sweet.

244
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:51,680
Rizal, you're awake.

245
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:53,667
Is there something you want?

246
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,140
Come closer.

247
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,860
What is it, friend?

248
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:01,240
I want a wife.

249
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,619
Hounding after the ladies even now.

250
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:04,800
Go to sleep.

251
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:08,800
This is bananas!

252
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:14,710
Carrot!

253
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:20,840
Hey, what's about it?

254
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:24,298
Duke Dogstorm and Master
Catviper have some big news.

255
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:26,362
They need you to come right now.

256
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:33,840
Ah, finally showed up,
huh? Hey, guys. What's up?

257
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:35,920
You got some news for me?

258
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,520
Why is everybody here?

259
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:39,520
You gotta keep us waiting.

260
00:17:56,880 --> 00:18:00,640
Carrot, we would like you, Kara,
to rule the Mokumo dukedom.

261
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:03,620
I get to roll!

262
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:05,390
Hooray!

263
00:18:05,473 --> 00:18:06,303
Works for me!

264
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,720
I can't do that!

265
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,160
Don't make me!

266
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:22,160
I would be awful, I swear!

267
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:27,180
The thing is, the Catanine
decided to stay in Wano.

268
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:29,577
We're still samurai of the Kozuki clan.

269
00:18:29,660 --> 00:18:32,425
So it is our duty to keep
Lord Momonosuke safe.

270
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:39,296
You, Karoo, have traveled with Luffy,

271
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:42,537
so you, Karoo, have a broader
view of the world than other Minx.

272
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:45,197
That's what the next
generation will need the most.

273
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,751
We believe in you, Karoo.

274
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:48,400
Oh, like me, though!

275
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:50,677
There's tons of Minx stronger than I am!

276
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:52,289
Should you ask them first?

277
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,397
No, they should not!

278
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,680
It is the duty of the strong
to protect our country!

279
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:00,811
I support their decision.

280
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:03,201
And I will support you, Tia, too.

281
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:14,580
Carrot, Yotia can do this.

282
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,861
Pedro's will lives in your heart.

283
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,280
Pedro's will?

284
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:25,285
We're counting on you, Carrot.

285
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:28,694
Tomorrow belongs to the young,
and so should Zoe, I say.

286
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:34,840
You really are grandfather?

287
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,237
Indeed.

288
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:40,360
Kozuki Odin was my son.

289
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:46,480
I'm so glad you're alive and well.

290
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:48,100
I'm sorry.

291
00:19:48,420 --> 00:19:51,420
I've been so ashamed that
I almost didn't tell you.

292
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:53,560
I couldn't save Odin after all.

293
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:59,260
What's worse, I couldn't save the
land of Wano despite being Shogun.

294
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:01,600
I failed you. Forgive me.

295
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:04,297
I have always wanted to meet you.

296
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:05,260
Me as well?

297
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:07,180
You're too kind.

298
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:09,840
I'm still shocked.

299
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:13,100
You look just like Odin did
at your age, Momonosuke.

300
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:14,536
I'm shocked as well.

301
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:18,080
But more than anything,
I'm happy to have a family.

302
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:21,717
You cannot know what that means
to us after our parents' loss.

303
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,329
So please don't apologize.

304
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:27,460
No matter what happened, we're so
glad to have you with us today.

305
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:40,620
My heart leapt into my throat
to think that he was among us.

306
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,100
I never dared to dream such a thing.

307
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:46,380
Lord Tsukiyaki is alive and well.

308
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:49,640
His disguise was truly flawless.

309
00:20:53,740 --> 00:20:57,340
I knew you'd figured out my
secret, but what was I to say?

310
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,360
You did wear a Tang mask.

311
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:01,277
I'm afraid that draws attention.

312
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:04,297
We certainly didn't think that
you were an average swordsmith.

313
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:07,851
We feigned ignorance out of
respect, but we weren't fooled.

314
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:10,180
Isn't that right, Master Keen?

315
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:13,660
Yes, of course!

316
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:15,997
My apologies.

317
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:17,780
I put you through so much.

318
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:22,044
I can tell you about the
land of Wano's history.

319
00:21:22,140 --> 00:21:24,964
I stayed alive all these
years so I could do so.

320
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:27,298
But that's all I'm good for anymore.

321
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:31,660
So I beg you, let me cede the throne
and let the nation think I'm dead.

322
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:34,100
This is a new era.

323
00:21:34,380 --> 00:21:36,200
It is yours to create.

324
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:38,616
Knowing that you are alive is enough.

325
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,133
That gives us strength.

326
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:52,317
You're telling me Pluton
is buried down there?

327
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,230
Yes.

328
00:21:53,313 --> 00:21:55,477
I didn't get to see it
in person, mind you.

329
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:56,680
But it is here.

330
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:59,640
I honestly wasn't even sure if it existed.

331
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:07,357
Is that the big ship Franky burned
the blueprints for correct an

332
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:11,837
ancient weapon with the name of
a god they said would you want to

333
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:17,257
have it Luffy the weapon no thanks
i'm good that's no surprise but

334
00:22:17,340 --> 00:22:22,740
after Odin traveled the seas he
wanted to unleash it i wonder why

335
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:24,710
What?! What?!

336
00:22:24,793 --> 00:22:25,680
I was in danger?!

337
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:28,220
Danger, you say?

338
00:22:28,460 --> 00:22:32,540
I suppose a mature woman like me
might strike you right in the heart.

339
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:34,940
Is that a joke? Who are you?

340
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:36,180
Who am I?

341
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:37,853
You don't recognize me?

342
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:41,814
I suppose I did waste away a
bit after that last battle.

343
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:44,920
But it's me, Shinobu.

344
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:46,550
What?!

345
00:22:47,460 --> 00:22:48,777
Whatever happened to you?

346
00:22:48,860 --> 00:22:49,697
I love it!

347
00:22:49,780 --> 00:22:53,020
You're so lovely, it shocked
me right down to my bones.

348
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:56,240
Although, I suppose bones are all I got.

349
00:22:58,640 --> 00:22:59,600
Bro, big bro!

350
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:01,760
Guess what?

351
00:23:02,140 --> 00:23:04,657
Shinobu's going to teach
me to be a real Kunoichi.

352
00:23:04,740 --> 00:23:09,564
I'll get real strong, so next time I see
you, you've got to let me join your crew.

353
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:11,682
Heck yeah, we could use a ninja.

354
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:13,180
So train hard.

355
00:23:15,020 --> 00:23:16,457
You bet I will.

356
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:19,720
I'm going to be a bewitching
Kunoichi in no time, bro.

357
00:23:20,580 --> 00:23:21,410
Ning, ning.

358
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:24,960
Otama, you are so precious.

359
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:29,080
Oh, I'm going to miss you most of all.

360
00:23:30,940 --> 00:23:32,740
Now there's a shocker.

361
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:35,020
Pluton is in the land of Wano?

362
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,800
First Poseidon, and now this.

363
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:42,515
I know a certain someone who's going
to be very interested in this news.

364
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:00,770
Shogun!

365
00:24:00,853 --> 00:24:02,200
I've been looking for you.

366
00:24:04,420 --> 00:24:05,960
The plans are complete.

367
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:08,401
Reconstruction can begin shortly.

368
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:09,700
That's good.

369
00:24:11,780 --> 00:24:15,480
I've included cost estimates
for each region as well. I see.

370
00:24:15,780 --> 00:24:16,662
Excellent work.

371
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:18,400
Shogun, sir!

372
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:21,557
We have proposals to repurpose
the weapons factories.

373
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:23,537
They're just waiting for your approval.

374
00:24:23,620 --> 00:24:24,920
Right. Let's go.

375
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:32,040
Excuse me.

376
00:24:32,420 --> 00:24:35,497
Can you give me your opinion on the
reservoir when you have the time?

377
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:37,737
We should speak with
all the daimyo as well.

378
00:24:37,820 --> 00:24:39,897
Let's schedule a meeting
in the near future.

379
00:24:39,980 --> 00:24:40,810
Of course.

380
00:24:43,040 --> 00:24:44,000
Hello, Shogun!

381
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:55,620
Hey, Zoro!

382
00:24:56,080 --> 00:24:58,297
I'd like to learn a few sword techniques.

383
00:24:58,380 --> 00:25:00,980
Do you think you could teach me? Hello?

384
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:05,040
Luffy! Zoro!

385
00:25:11,140 --> 00:25:12,060
Onami!

386
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:13,590
Usopp!

387
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:25,730
Sanchi?

388
00:25:25,813 --> 00:25:28,720
Chopper him on? Robin? Franky? Bonkichi?

389
00:25:29,120 --> 00:25:30,037
Are you there, Jinbei?

390
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:30,950
Yamato?

391
00:25:31,033 --> 00:25:32,997
Where did everyone go? Hello?

392
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:35,492
Hiyori, have you seen Luffy and his crew?

393
00:25:36,020 --> 00:25:37,549
They said their farewells.

394
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:39,856
They're leaving the land of Wano now.

395
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:41,840
Sad, huh?

396
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:47,040
Said their farewells?

397
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:49,206
They didn't say a word to me.

398
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,480
There you are, Lord Momonosuke! Yes?

399
00:25:54,700 --> 00:25:55,641
What's going on?

400
00:25:55,760 --> 00:25:57,160
Is this about Luffy?

401
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:59,457
I just found out that he's departing!

402
00:25:59,540 --> 00:26:00,370
You too?

403
00:26:00,453 --> 00:26:01,540
This is so cruel!

404
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:06,157
I asked all the retainers, and the Straw
Hat spoke to every one of them but me!

405
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:09,769
Why would they exclude us when
we've known them the longest?

406
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:28,077
We're leaving today you don't get
to huh what does that mean don't

407
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:31,977
make it weird all right We can't
all sail off at the same time

408
00:26:32,060 --> 00:26:36,697
our alliance is over remember
we're enemies now We're leaving

409
00:26:36,780 --> 00:26:41,920
today because that's what we decided
on so did we the hell Trafalgar

410
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:45,180
This is my day. Pick
another. Yeah, no thanks.

411
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:47,457
You can change your own damn schedule.

412
00:26:47,540 --> 00:26:49,187
Well, I'm not changing mine.

413
00:26:49,580 --> 00:26:51,698
This is nothing but a waste of time.

414
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:53,740
Fine. How's this?

415
00:26:54,100 --> 00:26:56,041
We'll go in different directions.

416
00:26:56,520 --> 00:26:59,257
The log poe's locked onto
three different islands.

417
00:26:59,340 --> 00:27:02,281
One is northeast, one's
east, and one's southeast.

418
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:03,820
Take your pick.

419
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:05,080
The metal hoist.

420
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:07,550
All right.

421
00:27:07,780 --> 00:27:09,074
It's your problem now.

422
00:27:09,660 --> 00:27:12,637
Heading northeast gets you
the farthest ahead, you know.

423
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:16,308
If you had half a brain cell
between you two, you'd get that.

424
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:19,140
The middle one?

425
00:27:20,980 --> 00:27:21,810
Dumbasses.

426
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:26,560
I don't care what you do,
because I'm heading off now.

427
00:27:26,860 --> 00:27:27,978
Have fun bickering.

428
00:27:28,620 --> 00:27:30,897
All right, Straw Hat, let's draw for it.

429
00:27:30,980 --> 00:27:33,157
When it goes east, lose it goes southeast.

430
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:34,440
I picked this one.

431
00:27:37,660 --> 00:27:38,490
Ha!

432
00:27:38,573 --> 00:27:39,700
I got east.

433
00:27:40,740 --> 00:27:42,480
I messed up the draw!

434
00:27:43,080 --> 00:27:44,880
I'm sorry, you guys!

435
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:48,520
Just help us load the sunny!

436
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:51,094
It's gonna be dangerous wherever we go!

437
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:52,300
So who cares?

438
00:27:52,620 --> 00:27:54,280
I'm an emperor of the sea!

439
00:27:54,560 --> 00:27:57,160
How could I lose it then? Huh?

440
00:27:57,720 --> 00:27:59,380
Now you're pissing me off!

441
00:27:59,780 --> 00:28:02,837
Still, there's one emperor
even lamer than you!

442
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:04,720
Can you believe this?

443
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:09,280
Buggy the Genius Jester.

444
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,980
What the heck?

445
00:28:26,220 --> 00:28:28,338
Crocodile and Hawkeye are there too.

446
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:29,470
Huh?

447
00:28:29,553 --> 00:28:31,677
They're making you look
like they work for Buggy.

448
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:32,590
What?

449
00:28:32,673 --> 00:28:33,857
There's no way that's right.

450
00:28:33,940 --> 00:28:36,116
Hawkeye wouldn't work for that clown.

451
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:41,280
If he really has those two under
his control, then I get it.

452
00:28:41,660 --> 00:28:44,189
That alone would make
him emperor material.

453
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:46,060
Bucky's just a dumbass.

454
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:47,673
How'd he pull this off?

455
00:28:47,820 --> 00:28:51,997
I couldn't tell you, but the new company
he's running is called Cross Guild,

456
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:55,157
and they've started putting bounties
on the heads of famous marines.

457
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:57,358
The Navy was always a hunter before,

458
00:28:57,560 --> 00:29:00,917
but now anyone in the world can come
after them just like us pirates.

459
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:04,471
It seems that while we were
on our little getaway in Wind,

460
00:29:04,700 --> 00:29:07,360
the entire world turned on its head.

461
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:13,609
Anyway, you know where
you're going, right?

462
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:18,602
Good thing we're headed in different
directions, because we're enemies from now on.

463
00:29:24,380 --> 00:29:25,840
This is a parting gift?

464
00:29:26,100 --> 00:29:27,276
What the hell is it?

465
00:29:27,480 --> 00:29:29,362
It's a copy of a road poneglyph.

466
00:29:29,820 --> 00:29:32,817
Poneglyph, you guys have
the right to this as well.

467
00:29:32,900 --> 00:29:35,135
Cheating would take the fun out of it.

468
00:29:35,540 --> 00:29:37,320
So Kaido did have one of them.

469
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:41,722
It's just like the thing we swiped
from one of Big Mom's generals.

470
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:45,129
We're in the endgame, kid.

471
00:29:45,260 --> 00:29:47,220
We gotta get serious about this.

472
00:29:47,780 --> 00:29:51,237
You know what we gotta do if we
wanna fight for the One Piece.

473
00:29:51,320 --> 00:29:53,377
Find the man with the burn scar, right?

474
00:29:53,460 --> 00:29:54,460
That's step one.

475
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,380
We don't have any leads, though. Huh?

476
00:29:58,020 --> 00:29:58,850
Huh?

477
00:29:58,933 --> 00:29:59,763
What burn scar?

478
00:29:59,846 --> 00:30:00,814
Where'd you hear that?

479
00:30:05,500 --> 00:30:06,900
You don't know?

480
00:30:07,920 --> 00:30:10,220
Looks like I get a head start, huh?

481
00:30:11,520 --> 00:30:13,440
Come on, just tell me!

482
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:15,830
Yamato!

483
00:30:15,913 --> 00:30:16,743
Are you here?

484
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:18,310
Yamato!

485
00:30:19,140 --> 00:30:21,620
You're not hiding from me, are you?

486
00:30:22,380 --> 00:30:23,210
Yamato!

487
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:26,320
Hey, Momonosuke!

488
00:30:26,760 --> 00:30:27,760
I'm up here!

489
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:29,640
Where is here?

490
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:33,200
On top of the roof, it would seem.

491
00:30:34,540 --> 00:30:35,370
All right.

492
00:30:35,580 --> 00:30:37,320
I've made up my mind.

493
00:30:46,780 --> 00:30:49,500
Luffy, this is it. I'm ready.

494
00:30:53,660 --> 00:30:54,490
Finally!

495
00:30:54,573 --> 00:30:56,960
I'm going to live like Kozuki Oden!
